+## One proposal, two different openings
 
-### What is actually in the package?
+Two saved **Profiler Plus** runs used the same synthetic museum-training offer. Olga, the finance recipient, asked for the full cost and equipment requirements first. Sofya, the programme recipient, prioritised accuracy and the author's voice.
 
-| Protocol | Operation | Concrete result |
-| --- | --- | --- |
-| **Profiler** | Map evidenced decision criteria, trusted grounds and possible barriers. | Bounded decision map, communication frame, alternatives and a useful next move. |
-| **Profiler Plus** | Explain an unchanged proposal through the recipient’s evidenced priorities. | Ready-to-use message with adapted argument order and preserved material terms. |
-| **Dopamine Hooks** | Develop attention and understanding through the whole text. | Complete connected text with meaningful answers; optional debug map. No neurochemical claims. |
-| **Reverse** | Walk through the text using only recipient-known context, then answer consequential questions. | Revised material with supported answers at their point of need, plus a compact change map. |
-| **Rail** | Prepare the actual execution kit within known human authority. | Ready request/table/calculations, complete handoff, relevant branches and explicit blockers. |
+**Olga — editorial English translation excerpt:**
 
-Each protocol has an operational specification, a standalone `SKILL.md`, an input/output contract, an example and synthetic evaluation cases. No mode starts the other four automatically.
